<header class="page-header">
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p>Last updated: September 14, 2026</p>
</header>

<p>This policy describes how SLP WOW (“we”, “the site”) handles information when you visit slpwow.com. It is written for clinicians browsing professional content, not for patient portals.</p>

<h2>Information we collect</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Usage data:</strong> standard web logs (IP address, browser type, pages viewed) if hosting is enabled.</li>
  <li><strong>Contact email:</strong> if you write to us, we keep correspondence needed to respond.</li>
  <li><strong>Forum accounts (future):</strong> when Discourse launches, account data will be governed by that platform’s settings plus this policy.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How we use information</h2>
<p>We use data to operate the site, measure aggregate traffic, respond to professional inquiries, and secure our services. We do not sell personal information.</p>

<h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
<p>We may use privacy-conscious analytics with minimal cookies. When enabled, a cookie banner will describe opt-out choices before non-essential tracking runs.</p>

<h2>Professional content</h2>
<p>Do not submit protected health information (PHI) through contact forms or future forum posts. Use de-identified scenarios only.</p>

<h2>Third parties</h2>
<p>Hosting, email, and (when live) Discourse may process data under their own terms. Links to external journal sites or downloads leave slpwow.com.</p>

<h2>Your choices</h2>
<p>Request access or deletion of contact email we hold by writing to <a href="mailto:{{ site.contactEmail }}">{{ site.contactEmail }}</a>. Some logs may be retained for security for a limited period.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>We will post updates on this page with a revised date. Material changes to forum processing will be announced before launch.</p>
